{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC8 residual RCA and close evidence\n\nRoot cause: AC8's oracle intentionally greps for the literal `0.12.7` across `pyproject.toml`, `Makefile`, and `scripts/check_uv_pin.py`, but `scripts/check_uv_pin.py:16-17` used concrete docstring examples (`==0.12.7` / `>=0.12.7`). Those examples were documentation, not a second pin, so the single-source guard failed by counting illustrative text.\n\nRED: before the docstring edit, `[ \"$(grep -rlF '0.12.7' pyproject.toml Makefile scripts/check_uv_pin.py | wc -l)\" -eq 1 ]` returned rc=1 with count=2 (`pyproject.toml` and `scripts/check_uv_pin.py`).\n\nFix: changed only the docstring examples to `==X.Y.Z` / `>=X.Y.Z`; guard logic and `pyproject.toml`'s `required-version = \"==0.12.7\"` pin were not changed.\n\nGREEN: after the edit, the same AC8 command returned rc=0 with count=1, and the only matching file is `pyproject.toml`. Additional validation passed: `python scripts/check_uv_pin.py`, `pytest tests/unit/test_uv_pin_guard.py` (11 passed), and `make lint`.\n\nDefect origin: plan/AC precision escape in this ticket's own pin work. The concrete docstring examples and AC8 literal grep were introduced by commit `7501cc1d602d` under `rebar-ticket: 56b7-b21a-c8ab-4afc`; the residual close blocker is therefore attributed by scope/history to `56b7-b21a-c8ab-4afc` as `plan_defect`.\n\nGerrit: change 2471 patch set 1 reached `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1` (GitHub run 33460691270), zero unresolved comments, and was submitted/merged as `e768151d680f7295bfd37424cec31946b88d0ab8`."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788230588353035001,"uuid":"607a56cb-4320-41b6-bcaf-e681e2eb9d33"}